{"author":{"id":"29588b87a98184856c6eb9104921c34cca98a9cb029a2ee86cc10622d693ba86"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794789514,"nonce":"klwMJrmx/wuHNkdjDONdUX4cxzw=","title":"rich_text_editor: follow external theme and style tokens","message":"Low priority, not blocking anything. `RichTextTheme` (`render.rs`) has a fixed set of optional colours and sizes. The widget does not follow the surrounding application's style: colours not set in `RichTextTheme` come from the `.blinc-rich-text*` CSS rules (`render.rs`), and the other values are fixed fields. The caret already falls back to `ColorToken::TextPrimary` (`content.rs:235`). An app with its own named styles cannot apply them to the editor by theme tokens alone.\n\nWould it be possible to build `RichTextTheme` from `blinc_theme` tokens (for example `ColorToken` values), and to accept a style or class name from the outer application, so that the editor's text, marker, quote, divider, code and selection colours all follow the program's style? Thank you for Blinc, and no rush on this.","files":null}]}